.TH ZION 1 "March 2026" "Zion 1.0.8" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
zion \- A modern, cargo-inspired package manager for the Zig programming language

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zion
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Zion
is a modern package manager for the Zig programming language that provides seamless dependency management with automatic build integration. It supports GitHub repositories and provides reproducible builds through lock files.

.SH COMMANDS

.SS Project Management

.TP
.B init
Initialize a new Zig project with necessary file structure

.TP
.B build
Build the project using the Zig build system

.TP
.B run
Build and run the project

.TP
.B test
Run project tests

.TP
.B clean \fR[\fI--all\fR] [\fI--cache\fR]
Remove build artifacts and caches. Use --all to remove everything including lock files, --cache to clear only cache

.TP
.B fmt
Format project source files

.TP
.B check
Check project for issues without building

.SS Dependency Management

.TP
.B add \fIPACKAGE\fR
Add a dependency to your project. PACKAGE should be in the format "username/repo" or a package name

.TP
.B remove \fIPACKAGE\fR, rm \fIPACKAGE\fR
Remove a dependency from your project with complete cleanup

.TP
.B update \fR[\fIPACKAGE\fR]
Update all dependencies or a specific package to their latest versions

.TP
.B fetch
Fetch all dependencies specified in your build.zig.zon file

.TP
.B list, ls \fR[\fI--json\fR]
List all dependencies in the project with their installation status. Use --json for machine-readable output

.TP
.B info \fIPACKAGE\fR
Show detailed information about a specific package dependency

.TP
.B search \fIQUERY\fR
Search for packages matching the query

.TP
.B outdated
Check for outdated dependencies

.TP
.B tree \fR[\fI--check-cycles\fR] [\fI--depth=N\fR] [\fI--duplicates\fR] [\fI--no-versions\fR]
Display dependency tree. Use --check-cycles to detect circular dependencies, --depth to limit depth, --duplicates to show duplicate packages, --no-versions to hide version info

.SS Version Pinning

.TP
.B pin \fIPACKAGE\fR \fIVERSION\fR
Pin a dependency to a specific version

.TP
.B unpin \fIPACKAGE\fR \fR[\fI--to-main\fR]
Unpin a dependency to allow updates. Use --to-main to track the default branch

.TP
.B lock
Update or create the lock file based on your build.zig.zon dependencies

.SS Package Integrity

.TP
.B hash \fR[\fIupdate\fR] [\fIPACKAGE\fR] [\fI--branch=NAME\fR]
Manage package hashes. Use "hash update" to refresh hashes, --branch to specify branch

.TP
.B sign \fIPACKAGE\fR
Sign a package with Ed25519 cryptographic signature

.TP
.B keyring \fR[\fIadd\fR|\fIlist\fR|\fIremove\fR]
Manage trusted public keys for package verification

.SS Zig Toolchain

.TP
.B zig \fR[\fIinstall\fR|\fIlist\fR|\fIuse\fR] [\fIVERSION\fR]
Manage Zig versions. Install, list, or switch between Zig versions

.TP
.B zls \fR[\fIinstall\fR|\fIupdate\fR]
Install or update the Zig Language Server

.SS Registry & Publishing

.TP
.B registry \fR[\fIlist\fR|\fIadd\fR|\fIremove\fR|\fIhealth\fR]
Manage package registries

.TP
.B publish
Publish a package to a registry

.SS Project Tools

.TP
.B doc
Generate documentation for the project

.TP
.B template \fR[\fIlist\fR|\fIcreate\fR|\fIapply\fR]
Manage project templates

.TP
.B workspace \fR[\fIinit\fR|\fIadd\fR|\fIlist\fR]
Manage multi-project workspaces

.TP
.B config \fR[\fIget\fR|\fIset\fR|\fIlist\fR]
View or modify Zion configuration

.TP
.B cache \fR[\fIclean\fR|\fIinfo\fR]
Manage package cache

.SS Utilities

.TP
.B status
Show project status summary

.TP
.B repair
Attempt to repair project issues

.TP
.B analyze
Analyze project dependencies and structure

.TP
.B version
Display the current version of Zion

.TP
.B help
Display help information about available commands

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.B --json
When used with list command, outputs machine-readable JSON format

.TP
.B --all
When used with clean command, removes all build artifacts including lock files

.TP
.B --cache
When used with clean command, removes only cached files

.TP
.B --check-cycles, -c
When used with tree command, detect circular dependencies

.TP
.B --depth=N
When used with tree command, limit tree display depth

.TP
.B --duplicates
When used with tree command, show duplicate dependencies

.TP
.B --no-versions
When used with tree command, hide version information

.TP
.B --to-main
When used with unpin command, track the repository's default branch

.TP
.B --branch=NAME
When used with hash update, specify branch to use

.SH EXAMPLES

.TP
Initialize a new project:
.B zion init

.TP
Add a dependency:
.B zion add mitchellh/libxev

.TP
List dependencies:
.B zion list

.TP
Remove a dependency:
.B zion remove libxev

.TP
Update all dependencies:
.B zion update

.TP
Show dependency tree:
.B zion tree

.TP
Check for circular dependencies:
.B zion tree --check-cycles

.TP
Update package hash:
.B zion hash update libxev

.TP
Pin to default branch:
.B zion unpin libxev --to-main

.TP
Clean build artifacts:
.B zion clean

.TP
Complete cleanup:
.B zion clean --all

.TP
Install specific Zig version:
.B zion zig install 0.16.0

.TP
Search for packages:
.B zion search http

.SH FILES

.TP
.I build.zig.zon
Project manifest file containing metadata and dependencies

.TP
.I zion.lock
Lock file ensuring reproducible builds with exact dependency versions

.TP
.I .zion/cache/
Directory containing downloaded package tarballs

.TP
.I .zion/deps/
Directory containing extracted package sources

.SH ENVIRONMENT

Zion respects the following environment variables:

.TP
.B ZIG_PATH
Override the path to the Zig executable

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Success

.TP
.B 1
General error

.TP
.B 2
File not found

.TP
.B 3
Invalid command usage

.SH REQUIREMENTS

.TP
- Zig 0.16.0 or newer
.TP
- curl (for downloading packages)
.TP
- tar (for extracting packages)
.TP
- git (for some operations)

